// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 21-standard-library-semantics
// facility: rule.stdlib.swap [Swap-Places] [Swap-Places-Conflict]; D-0235; conf.swap-passed-ref-beside-shared-reborrow
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.aliasing-conflict (static)
//
// `r` is passed on whole to `swap`, which forms no borrow, while `s`, a
// shared reborrow of `*r`, lives. `[Swap-Places]` writes `*r` as `[Write]`
// would (D-0235), and `s` is a live conflicting path, so the exchange faults.
// Before D-0235 it ran, and `s` read 2: a shared reference saw what it
// reaches change.
//
// D-0282: the static pass rejects this program before it runs (it was found
// at run time before): `swap` writes `*r` through argument 1 while `s`
// still borrows `*r`.

import std;

fn main()
{
    i32 x = 1;
    i32 y = 2;
    auto r = &mut x;
    auto s = &*r;
    swap(r, &mut y);
    printf("%v %v\n", *s, y);
}
